          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystal"} crystalline
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+material"} quantum material
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy+gap"} gapped
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+state"} ground state
            is said to be in a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+phase+of+matter"} topological phase
            if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bloch+Hamiltonian"} Bloch Hamiltonian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/map"} map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mover
                    %mi T
                    %mo ^
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{(-)} \colon \widehat{T}{}^d \longrightarrow \mathscr{A}
            (from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brillouin+torus"} Brillouin torus
            of crystal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/momenta"} momenta
            to the space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{A}
            of accessible individual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonians"} Hamiltonians
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mover
                          %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{[\vec k]}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+class"} homotopy class
          %p
            Whether and how this is the case depends crucially on the choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{A}
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{A}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{A}
          %p
            In the extreme case one allows the system to undergo deformations during which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electrons"} electrons
            may occupy arbitrarily high
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy+bands"} energy bands
            %em coarsest
            resolution of the situation gives the most
            %em stable
            classification. This is the situation most commonly considered, notably in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+topological+phases+of+matter"} K-theory classification of topological phases of matter
          %p
            All other classifications are
            = succeed "." do
              %em unstable
            %em fragile
            (
            %a{:href => "#PWV18"}> PWV 2018
            ) or
            %em delicate
            (
            %a{:href => "#NNBA21"}> NNBA 2021
            ):
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em fragile
                band topology: unstable when accessing further
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conduction+bands"} conduction bands
            %li
              %p
                %em delicate
                band topology: unstable when accessing further
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conduction+bands"} conduction bands
                or
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valence+bands"} valence bands
                (generally: both types).
          %p
            In mathematical terminology, unstable topological phased are classified (
            %a{:href => "#SatiSchreiber25"}> SS 2025
            ) by the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"}> equivariant
            )
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi T
                    %mo ^
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %mo ;
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒜
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi Map
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi T
                    %mo ^
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒜
                  %msup
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H_G\big(\widehat{T}{}^d; \mathscr{A} \big)
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\pi_0 Map\big(\widehat{T}{}^d, \mathscr{A} \big)^G
          %p
            (of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brillouin+torus"} Brillouin torus
            with respect to the crystal’s
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+group"} point group
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+spaces"} classifying spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{A}
            that are indeed unstable in the sense of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+loop+spaces"} infinite loop spaces
            (not stages of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            of spaces).
          %h2#Details Details
          %h3#the_classifying_space The classifying space
          %p The assumption that the system and all its accessible deformations are
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy+gap"} gapped
            %li
              %p
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in \mathbb{N}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valence+bands"} valence bands
                filled
            %li
              %p
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \mathbb{N}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conduction+bands"} conduction bands
                available
          %p
            means that the space of available
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bloch+Hamiltonians"} Bloch Hamiltonians
            is (taking the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy+gap"} energy gap
            to be around zero, without restriction of generality)
          #eq:SpaceOfAccessibleBlochHamiltonians.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AccBlchHams
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} {
                  %mi H
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo +
                      %mi c
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo †
                  %mo =
                  %mi H
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Eig
                    %mrow
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mi v
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Eig
                    %mrow
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mi c
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  AccBlchHams
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\Big\{
                  H \in \mathcal{B}\big(\mathbb{C}^{v+c}\big)
                  \\,\Big\vert\,
                  H^\dagger = H
                  ,\,
                  Eig_{\lt 0}(H) \simeq \mathbb{C}^{v}
                  ,\,
                  Eig_{\gt 0}(H) \simeq \mathbb{C}^c
                  \\Big\}
                  \\,,
          %p where
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℬ
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mrow
                          %mi v
                          %mo +
                          %mi c
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi Mat
                        %mrow
                          %mi v
                          %mo +
                          %mi c
                          %mo ×
                          %mi v
                          %mo +
                          %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}\big(\mathbb{C}^{v+c}\big) \simeq Mat_{v+c \times v + c}(\mathbb{C})
                denotes the space of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+linear+operators"} bounded linear operators
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrices"} matrices
            %li
              %p
                “
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Eig
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msup
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mrow
                          %mi v
                          %mo +
                          %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Eig_{(-)}(H) \subset \mathbb{C}^{v+c}
                ” denotes the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenspace"} eigenspace
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"} Hamiltonian
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+operator"} operator
                for the given range of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenvalues"} eigenvalues
          %p
            Since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maps"} maps
            to this space depend only on its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SpaceOfAccessibleBlochHamiltonians"} (1)
            is evidently
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalent
            to the space of
            %em normalized
            Bloch Hamiltonians whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenvalues"} eigenvalues
            have unit
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+value"} absolute value
          #eq:SpaceOfNormalizedBlochHamiltonians.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi NrmAccBlchHams
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} {
                  %mi H
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo +
                      %mi c
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo †
                  %mo =
                  %mi H
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Eig
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mi v
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Eig
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mi c
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  NrmAccBlchHams
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\Big\{
                  H \in \mathcal{B}\big(\mathbb{C}^{v+c}\big)
                  \\,\Big\vert\,
                  H^\dagger = H
                  ,\,
                  Eig_{-1}(H) \simeq \mathbb{C}^{v}
                  ,\,
                  Eig_{+1}(H) \simeq \mathbb{C}^c
                  \\Big\}
                  \\,,
          %p via
          #eq:HomotopyEquivalenceNormalizingBlochHamiltonians.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mi AccBlchHams
                      %mtd
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mphantom
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo ∼
                            %mphantom
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mtd
                        %mi NrmAccBlchHams
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mi H
                      %mtd
                        %mo ↦
                      %mtd
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mi H
                        %mo ≔
                        %msup
                          %msqrt
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi H
                                %mn 2
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi H
                        %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                          %mrow
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{array}{ccc}
                  AccBlchHams
                  \&amp;\xrightarrow{\phantom{-} \sim  \phantom{-}}&amp;
                  NrmAccBlchHams
                  \\\
                  H
                  \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                  N_H \coloneqq \sqrt{H^2}^{-1} \circ H
                  \\mathrlap{\,,}
                  \\end{array}
          %p where
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msqrt
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi H
                            %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqrt{H^2}
                denotes the unique
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+definite+matrix"} positive definition
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/square+root"} square root
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^{-1}
                denotes the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} inverse
                operator.
          %p
            In fact,
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:HomotopyEquivalenceNormalizingBlochHamiltonians"} (3)
            is a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+retraction"} deformation retraction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+inverse"} right inverse
            is given by the inclusion
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mi NrmAccBlchHams
                      %mtd
                        %mover
                          %mo ↪
                          %mphantom
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mo −
                      %mtd
                        %mi AccBlchHams
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mi N
                      %mtd
                        %mo ↦
                      %mtd
                        %mi N
                        %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                          %mrow
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{array}{ccc}
                  NrmAccBlchHams
                  \&amp;\xhookrightarrow{\phantom{--}}&amp;
                  AccBlchHams
                  \\\
                  N &amp;\mapsto&amp; N
                  \\mathrlap{\,,}
                  \\end{array}
          %p
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (H \mapsto N_H) \Rightarrow (H \mapsto H)
          %p is given by
          #eq:NormalizingHomotopy.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mi AccBlchHams
                        %mo ×
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtd
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mtd
                        %mi AccBlchHams
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi H
                        %mo ,
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtd
                        %mo ↦
                      %mtd
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo −
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msup
                          %msqrt
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi H
                                %mn 2
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %mi t
                        %msub
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} I
                          %mrow
                            %mi c
                            %mo +
                            %mi v
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi H
                        %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                          %mrow
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{array}{ccc}
                  AccBlchHams \times [0,1]
                  \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                  AccBlchHams
                  \\\
                  (H, t)
                  \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                  \\big(
                  (1-t)\sqrt{H^2}^{-1} + t \mathrm{I}_{c+v}
                  \\big)
                  \\circ
                  H
                  \\mathrlap{\,.}
                  \\end{array}
          %p
            But this space of normalized Bloch Hamiltonians
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SpaceOfNormalizedBlochHamiltonians"} (2)
            is furthermore
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalent
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"}> homeomorphic
            , even) to the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hermitian+operator"} hermitian
            = succeed "=" do
              %a{:href => "rank#RankOfALinearMap"} rank
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            %a{:href => "projection#InLinearAlgebra"} projection operators
          #eq:SpaceOfProjectors.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (5)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Proj
                    %mi v
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo +
                      %mi v
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} {
                  %mi P
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo +
                      %mi c
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mo †
                  %mo =
                  %mi P
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi P
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi P
                  %mo =
                  %mi P
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi rnk
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} }
                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Proj_v^{c+v}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\Big\{
                  P \in \mathcal{B}\big(\mathbb{C}^{v+c}\big)
                  \\,\Big\vert\,
                  P^\dagger = P
                  ,\,
                  P \circ P = P
                  ,\,
                  rnk(P) = c
                  \\Big\}
                  \\mathrlap{\,,}
          %p via
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mi NrmAccBlchHams
                      %mtd
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mphantom
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo ∼
                            %mphantom
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mtd
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Proj
                          %mi v
                          %mrow
                            %mi v
                            %mo +
                            %mi c
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mi N
                      %mtd
                        %mo ↦
                      %mtd
                        %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                          %mfrac
                            %mn 1
                            %mn 2
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mi c
                            %mo +
                            %mi v
                        %mo +
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                          %mrow
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{array}{ccc}
                  NrmAccBlchHams
                  \&amp;\xrightarrow{\phantom{-} \sim \phantom{-}}&amp;
                  Proj_{v}^{v+c}
                  \\\
                  N
                  \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                  \\tfrac{1}{2}\big(1_{c+v} + N\big)
                  \\mathrlap{}
                  \\end{array}
          %p
            and furthermore to the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmannian+space"}> Grassmannian space
            ”
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Gr
                    %mi v
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo +
                      %mi c
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} {
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo +
                      %mi c
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi dim
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi v
                      %mo +
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
