                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy"} Cohomotopy
          %h3#stabilization Stabilization
          %p
            The stable situation is obtained by allowing access to
            %em any
            number of conduction bands and valence bands.
          %p
            First, allowing access to arbitrary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conduction+bands"} conduction bands
            means to consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"}> colimit
            ) of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmannians"} Grassmannians
            with respect to their canonical inclusions
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Gr
                      %mi v
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo +
                        %mi c
                    %mo ↪
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Gr
                      %mi v
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo +
                        %mi c
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gr_v^{v + c} \hookrightarrow Gr_v^{v + c + 1}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                        %mrow
                          %mi c
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Gr
                      %mi v
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo +
                        %mi c
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  B \mathrm{U}(v)
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  \\textstyle{\bigcup_{c \in \mathbb{N}}}
                  Gr_v^{v + c}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This yields the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundles"} complex vector bundles
            of
            = succeed "=" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank+of+a+vector+bundle"} rank
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valence+bundle"} valence bundle
          %p
            The corresponding classifying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            theory
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:UnstablePhasesViaEquivariantNonabelianCohomology"} (7)
            is also known as
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unstable+K-theory"} unstable K-theory
          %p
            Then also allowing an arbitrary number of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valence+bands"} valence bands
            means to further pass to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"}> colimit
            )
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                        %mrow
                          %mi v
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                    %mi B
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Gr
                      %mi v
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo +
                        %mi c
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  B \mathrm{U}
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  \\textstyle{\bigcup_{v \in \mathbb{N}}}
                  B \mathrm{U}(v)
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  \\bigcup_{v \in \mathbb{N}}
                  \\bigcup_{c \in \mathbb{N}}
                  Gr_v^{v + c}
                  \\,,
          %p
            which is known as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+unitary+group"} stable unitary group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+K-theory"} reduced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+K-theory"} complex K-theory
            (of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/virtual+vector+bundles"} virtual vector bundles
            with vanishing virtual rank).
          %h2#references References
          %div
            %h3#ReferencesUnstableClassificationOfTopologicalPhases Unstable classification of topological phases
            %p
              Arguments for
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unstable+topological+phases+of+matter"} unstable topological phases of matter
